// the new keys walk.goodnight.friday.1 and .2; nothing sets them yet, so nothing changes until then.
== week1
? flag:walk.goodnight.friday.1
- Fridays we knock off at half three.
? flag:walk.goodnight.friday.2
- Captain talks to all of us at four, then dinner.

// ======== into content/lines/halloran-emeka.lines (@crew halloran-emeka)
// ---- EW1 (events writer), short Fridays part E: Day 5 at 13:00, after he hands you your mug (d5-mug), said in order
// as bubbles while you're in the tea corner, only when SHORT_FRIDAY is on (the onboarding engineer's new keys
// beat.d5-friday.1-3; nothing sets them yet). The plan's wording, split to bubbles of 60 or fewer.
== week1
? flag:beat.d5-friday.1
- Short day today. Half three, clock out.
? flag:beat.d5-friday.2
- Then the auditorium at four. Deck R. She'll say your name.
? flag:beat.d5-friday.3
- Don't hide. Have a biscuit first. Have you eaten?   #funny

// ======== a new file, content/banks/fridays.lines (as below, from its @bank line)
@bank all
// EW1 (events writer), short Fridays part E (plans/fridays-plan.md): now and then a crew member says it at Friday
// breakfast. flag:shortFriday is a new key (the traditions or sim engineer sets it while SHORT_FRIDAY is on), so these
// stay silent until then. Bubbles: 60 characters. Not in your first week: week 1 has its own lines (Zeke, Halloran).
== smalltalk
? weekday:fri act:breakfast flag:shortFriday !week1:true
- Short one today.
- Half three, then the Captain.
- Short Friday. I've planned my whole afternoon. It's a nap.   #funny
- Captain at four. I'm sitting at the back. Again.   #funny
- Friday. Half a day's work and a whole speech.   #funny
